  "notes": [
    "Development evidence is cumulative working-tree implementation evidence, not a new immutable remote release attestation or human UX PASS.",
    "Forge and Fabric final-JAR smoke preceded the final stale-admission/OPERATE-Presence guard tightening; those changes were subsequently unit-tested and rebuilt on all five Targets. NeoForge development smokes used the tightened code.",
    "All five automated smokes used only Runtime APIs; no host keyboard/mouse/window injection was used. Standard Minecraft Save & Quit in isolated test worlds is not a Persistent Write RPC.",
    "Supported boundaries are Minecraft/Loader standard callbacks, polling and render paths. Non-cooperative native Mods replacing GLFW callbacks or rendering after present are not sandboxed.",
    "Legacy split mouse-down/up is a Lease-owned raw stream; high-level gestures reject POINTER_HELD until it is released. Cleanup failure fail-closes the queue rather than risking handoff.",
    "Presence, Mode, Human Override, Lease, Debug Arm and Evidence Authority remain separate. Physical Esc/reconsent policy is unchanged from Round 1."
  ],
